      "displayName": "A. Soroka",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A24c578cc-15e9-4649-9f68-5eace85735e0",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>It looks to me like the code of interest is in:</p>\n\n<p>org.fcrepo.server.messaging.AtomAPIMMessage.objectToString(Object obj, String xsdType)</p>\n\n<p>where, at line 269, the serialization ends before accounting for xsd:base64Binary datatypes.</p>\n\n<p>I would be happy to work up a patch which checked for some appropriately-named parameter on the Messaging module config (e.g. \"includeBase64\") and if desired, serialized base64 values into exactly that- base64 values. If I have time, I'll be happy to try for a filtering arrangement wherein an additional parameter can be offered (e.g. \"onlyIfSmallerThan\", but better-named </p>\n{grin}\n<p>).</p>",
     "created": "27/Jan/11 10:58 PM",
     "id": "11793",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10802/comment/11793",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "557058:24c578cc-15e9-4649-9f68-5eace85735e0",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
