      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A24c578cc-15e9-4649-9f68-5eace85735e0",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Actually, I may be wrong, but perhaps it would be best to offer a switch to just try to encode anything that doesn't meet the earlier tests in that method as base64, instead of picking out those that originally were? I'm not clear as to whether payloads for REST ingest and modifyDatastreamByValue have that metadata, and those are the two very things I would want to catch.</p>",
