  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": "<p>As per the Messaging module documentation, the Atom messages emitted over JMS in connection with API-M calls include <em>almost</em> everything one would need to recreate the call. Except:</p>\n\n<p>'• Each &lt;category&gt; corresponds to a method's argument:</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>The term indicates the argument value. However, null values are indicated as \"null\", and non-null xsd:base64Binary values are indicated as \"<span class=\"error\">&#91;OMITTED&#93;</span>\".'</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>-from <a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FCR30/Messaging\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FCR30/Messaging</a></p>\n\n<p>so that a message consumer has almost, but not quite enough information to know exactly what happened in the case of 'ingest' and 'modifyDatastreamByValue' calls. It would be better to allow JMS messages to contain a full report of the method call. I understand that this could produce some really large messages, so it would be best to allow this as a configurable option.</p>",
